        "original_id": "2db7ef1b-ddec-5cca-af09-f28026d8ae47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Neleus of Scepsis, Aristotle, Theophrastus\n- Organizations: Peripatetic school\n- Places: Scepsis, Eresos, Lesbos\n- Roles: disciple, successor, executor\n- Concepts: library bequest\n\nFacts:\n- Theophrastus was a Greek native of Eresos in Lesbos who lived circa 371 to circa 287 BC.\n- Theophrastus succeeded Aristotle in the Peripatetic school.\n- Neleus of Scepsis was a disciple of Aristotle and Theophrastus.\n- Theophrastus bequeathed his library to Neleus of Scepsis and appointed Neleus as one of his executors.",
